<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="34ce03ba-8c83-5b08-8246-76d2bd8c2d23" activityNameId="27d36d17-0e21-5a55-aeba-0b45a9b229f7" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Electricity, wood, at distillery</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Electricity, wood, at distillery
Inventory refers to the production of 1 kg hydrated ethanol 95% (dry basis, i.e. 1.05 kg hydrated ethanol 95% wet basis), respectively 1 kWh of electricity from wood (u=70%, i.e. 59% dry matter). The multioutput-process 'wood, in distillery' delivers the co-products 'ethanol, 95% in H2O, from wood, at distillery' and 'electricity, from wood, at distillery'. Economic allocation with allocation factor for common stages of 99.7% to ethanol.;
UUID: ca57dde7-86e2-39af-9c0b-103001fe831b
This dataset includes the transport of wood from the forest to the distillery, and the processing of wood (u=70%) to hydrated ethanol (95%) and electricity. System boundary is at the distillery. Dehydration to anhydrous ethanol is not included. Process heat and power supply is ensured by the combustion of unconverted solids.
Location: Data is adapted to Swedish conditions from NREL ethanol process design from yellow poplar (1999) and information from alcosuisse
Technology: Ethanol is produced by dilute acid pre-hydrolysis and simultaneous saccharification and co-fermentation (SSCF) of lignocellulosic biomass. Process heat and power supply is ensured by the combustion of unconverted solids. Excess electricity is exported to the power grid.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: unknown 
Extrapolations: Literature data. 
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_ca57dde7-86e2-39af-9c0b-103001fe831b.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="742ea452-def3-5572-8ad0-bf9058ef212d" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
